-Electrostatic force : push and pull : F⃗ 
also called Coulomb’s force, 
arises between charged particles due to their electric charges. 
It is a fundamental interaction in nature 
and is part of the electromagnetic force, 
one of the four fundamental forces in the universe. 
The force can be attractive if the charges are opposite, 
or repulsive if the charges are the same (both positive or both negative) and acts along the line joining the charges

